  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A large dome of high pressure continues\nto grip the SW CONUS keeping high temperatures well above normal.\nAfternoon highs 10-15 degrees above normal have prompted an Extreme \nHeat Warning for Eastern Elko County and a Heat Advisory for the \nremainder of Northern and Central Nevada today through Sunday. Time \noutdoors should be limited for both people and animals. Those that \nwork outside should prioritize hydration. \n\nA slightly tighter pressure gradient in zonal flow just north of the \nSilver State will increase westerly wind speeds across the northern \nborder Friday through Sunday. Afternoon breezes combined with very \nlow RH values and extreme heat will create elevated fire weather \nconditions across Northern Nevada Friday through Sunday. \n\nFriday and Saturday, the positioning of the surface high will \nmeander eastward into the region of the Four Corners. This will open \nCentral and Southern NV up somewhat to monsoonal flow. Current \nguidance has Western AZ and the Baja being the main source regions \nfor moisture. While precipitable water values aren't spectacular \n(0.7-0.9 inches), the threat of convection will return to northern \nportions of Nye and Southern White Pine Counties possibly as soon as \nFriday. Diurnal forcing and sufficient instability make the threat \nof more dry than wet convection a possibility, though current \nprobabilities for storm activity remain low. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence continues for near \nrecord heat the remainder of the week. Moderate confidence exists in \nelevated fire weather conditions across Northern NV Friday through \nSunday. Low confidence remains in dry storm activity over Nye and \nWhite Pine Counties this weekend. No major changes needed for grids \nat this time.",
